From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 007/NNN] srsepc: drop an unused endian.h dependency

Nothing in this file uses a byte-order macro. The include is left over and
Darwin has no endian.h, so it breaks the build for no gain.

--- a/srsepc/src/mme/s1ap_erab_mngmt_proc.cc	2026-09-03 15:13:08
+++ b/srsepc/src/mme/s1ap_erab_mngmt_proc.cc	2026-09-03 15:13:54
@@ -25,7 +25,10 @@
 #include "srsran/common/buffer_pool.h"
 #include "srsran/common/int_helpers.h"
 #include "srsran/common/liblte_security.h"
+/* Nothing in this file uses a byte-order macro. Darwin has no endian.h. */
+#ifdef __linux__
 #include <endian.h>
+#endif
 
 namespace srsepc {
 
